      "id": "classic_00961",
      "title": "The Raggedy Man",
      "author": "James Whitcomb Riley",
      "difficulty": "hard",
      "theme": "The Goodest Man Ever You Saw",
      "category": "Joy & Whimsy",
      "poem_stanzas": [
        "O the Raggedy Man! He works fer Pa;\nAn' he's the goodest man ever you saw!\nHe comes to our house every day,\nAn' waters the horses, an' feeds 'em hay;\nAn' he opens the shed—an' we all ist laugh\nWhen he drives out our little ol' wobble-ly calf;\nAn' nen—ef our hired girl says he can—\nHe milks the cow fer 'Lizabuth Ann.—\nAin't he a' awful good Raggedy Man?\nRaggedy! Raggedy! Raggedy Man!"
      ],
